From 1d5d3227955dc711fd0adaa6adba9840548e9635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:26:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 248/269] Unified: find any tool by typing (Ctrl+K)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tool search opens with Ctrl+K, the field at the top right or Help ›
Search Tools. It finds every command of every module, also of modules not
loaded yet, by its Japanese or English name, other words for it
(CommandAliases.py: names in other CAD programs, the words the glossary
replaced) and its description. Of equally good matches, those that work
with the current selection and those of the everyday modules come first.
Each row says where the tool is. Picking a tool of a module that is not
loaded loads the module first (its commands only; the screen stays the
same). When nothing fits, the last row hands the question to the AI chat.

The catalog (CommandCatalog.json) is made at build time by the built
FreeCAD without a screen (make_catalog.py: all workbenches loaded, their
menus and toolbars read, texts in Japanese); the copy in the sources is
used when that cannot be done. Ranking and catalog are tested headless:
FreeCADCmd -t TestCommandSearch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
